# Database dumps written by the production stack's `/backups` mount. Never
# committed: they are the whole database, secrets and customer data included.
backups/

.vercel/

# ---- Editors / OS ----
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Uploaded documents. Never committed: they are customer data, and they are the
# supporting evidence for ledger entries, so they belong in the backup story
# (rsync the directory) rather than in version control.
backend/var/
credentials.json
token.pickle

# Microsoft's Visual C++ redistributable, bundled into the Windows installer. ~25 MB
# of someone else's binary, so it is fetched rather than committed - installer/README.md
# says where from, and the .iss fails the compile with that URL when it is absent.
#
# A glob rather than the filename: Microsoft ships it as `VC_redist.x64.exe`, this repo
# has referred to it in lower case, and Windows treats those as the same file while a
# case-sensitive checkout does not. Nothing else in that folder is an executable - the
# installer output goes to `installer/dist/`, ignored above.
installer/*.exe
# Rendered demo video. ~14 MB of binary that GitHub already hosts: the launch video is
# uploaded as a release-style attachment and the README embeds that URL, so a committed
# copy would be a second, heavier source of the same bytes - and a re-render would add
# another 14 MB to the history rather than replacing it.
#
# The source compositions in `videos/stellar-erp-launch/` are text and *are* committed,
# so every frame stays re-renderable; only the output is ignored.
docs/videos/
